MoE adapters on instance-normalized TSFMs fail because the normalization needed for distribution shift also strips the per-window statistics the router needs; raw pre-normalization routing fixes the failure, motivates Residual-IA\textsuperscript{+}, and $R(\mathcal{D})$ identifies where it applies. More broadly: when a foundation model's input pipeline destroys signal a downstream router needs, the fix is restoring the input rather than retuning the optimizer (replicated in a vision control, Appendix~\ref{app:vision_moe}). \textbf{Limits:} \emph{(i)}~our diagnosis covers instance-level normalization only (attention-based and learned normalizers uncharacterized); \emph{(ii)}~$R(\mathcal{D})$ is a single monotone proxy, not sharp on shape-statistics-coupled data (Solar, $R{=}0.06$); \emph{(iii)}~forecasting and imputation only.

\label{page:end_main}

